			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://pleroma.envs.net/objects/4d2bd38b-51ce-4d2c-b476-d3b295d1f80f",
			"author": {
				"name": "Seirdy",
				"url": "https://pleroma.envs.net/users/Seirdy",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/298/507/110/256/734/original/763ba80184ca4e95.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-15T23:16:46.126Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a class=\"u-url mention\" href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Not all clients are browsers, so no. Then there’s not just image viewing programs, but also image thumbnailers, messaging apps…</p><p>If you sent an image to get printed on an ID card, how likely do you think it is to work with WebP? Hell, Bing can barely handle PNG favicons.</p><p>I wouldn’t expect WebP to be supported by default.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
