			"author": {
				"name": "Khoi :platopunk:",
				"url": "https://platopunk.com/@khoi",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-16T05:02:53.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@sil\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>sil</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> why?</p><p>My blog (<a href=\"https://blog.imkhoi.com\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">https://blog.imkhoi.com</a>) current uses .WEBP and has had no issues. Most browsers support .WEBP nowadays.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111419373216020045",
			"parentId": "111418472767107219",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@sil/111419373141298457",
			"author": {
				"name": "Stuart Langridge",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@sil",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/302/147/382/032/479/original/ab95a50a2e58e997.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-11-16T08:51:52.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://platopunk.com/@khoi\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>khoi</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> ...exactly because you used the word \"most\" there, is why :) I agree; it'd probably be fine to use webp alone everywhere, but being sure of that is hard. I am sure of it for pngs and jpegs. So, if I put any effort into thinking about this question whatsoever, I might as well put that effort into using both inside a &lt;picture&gt;, and that's what I do.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
