		{
			"id": "111576268527747793",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://social.treehouse.systems/@lonjil/111576267559054643",
			"author": {
				"name": "lonjil",
				"url": "https://social.treehouse.systems/@lonjil",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2023-12-14T01:52:11.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> apologies for barging in on an old post like this, but I believe jpegli, a new jpeg encoder from the JXL people, will be released next year. In what testing I've done and seen from other people, the JPEGs it produces are smaller and higher quality than what cwebp can do. So to me even if webp is a safe choice, I see little reason to use it when legacy jpeg continues to improve year after year.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
